cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHON in academic work, please cite this repository."
title: "PHON: Phononic Orchestration Notation"
abstract: >-
  A declarative DSL for programming phononic (acoustic) computing circuits.
  Programs specify physical media, wave components, and signal flow using
  frequencies, phases, and amplitudes. Includes a reference simulator
  (idealized complex amplitude and 1D FDTD) and an LLM-assisted code
  generation pipeline. The specification is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0;
  the reference implementation under Apache 2.0.
authors:
  - name: "The PHON Authors"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: "Apache-2.0"
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
# TODO: Replace with your actual repository URL before publishing
repository-code: "https://github.com/Popisone/PHON"
keywords:
  - phononics
  - acoustic computing
  - DSL
  - declarative programming
  - wave interference
  - FDTD
  - computational physics